{"name":"Couch Potato","hex":"#c2b4a7","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"couch potato","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A person who spends a lot of time sitting or lying down, often watching television, eating snacks or drinking alcohol. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/couch_potato"}],"entries":[{"title":"Couch potato","blocks":[{"text":"A couch potato is a person who spends most of their free time sitting or lying on a couch. This stereotype often refers to a lazy and overweight person who watches a great deal of television. Generally speaking, the term refers to a lifestyle in which children or adults do not get enough physical activity."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ad/Frontliner_Couch_Potato-01.svg/330px-Frontliner_Couch_Potato-01.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Couch_potato"},{"title":"Couch Potato (TV series)","blocks":[{"text":"Couch Potato is an Australian children's television show broadcast on ABC TV in Australia and a staple of Classic ABC."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Couch_Potato_(TV_series)"},{"title":"Couch","blocks":[{"text":"A couch, also known as a sofa, settee, chesterfield, or davenport, is a cushioned piece of furniture that can seat multiple people. It is commonly found in the form of a bench with upholstered armrests and is often fitted with springs and tailored cushion and pillows. Although a couch is used primarily for seating, it may be used for sleeping. In homes, couches are normally put in the family room, living room, den, or lounge. They are sometimes also found in non-residential settings such as hotels, lobbies of commercial offices, waiting rooms, and bars. Couches can also vary in size, color, and design."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c2/2009-05-16_Main_office_lobby_at_Hampton_Forest_Apartments.jpg/330px-2009-05-16_Main_office_lobby_at_Hampton_Forest_Apartments.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Couch"},{"title":"Potato","blocks":[{"text":"The potato is a starchy tuberous vegetable native to the Americas that is consumed as a staple food in many parts of the world. Potatoes are underground stem tubers of the plant Solanum tuberosum, a perennial in the nightshade family Solanaceae."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ab/Patates.jpg/330px-Patates.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Potato"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/Loriots_Sofa.JPG/500px-Loriots_Sofa.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/Loriots_Sofa.JPG/1280px-Loriots_Sofa.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/Loriots_Sofa.JPG/500px-Loriots_Sofa.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Loriot's sofa at the Deutsche Kinemathek museum, 2012","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALoriots_Sofa.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Wedding_Couch.jpg/500px-Wedding_Couch.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Wedding_Couch.jpg/1280px-Wedding_Couch.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Wedding_Couch.jpg/500px-Wedding_Couch.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Wedding Couch, Asansol, West Bengal, India","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/F